s":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Neither gift nor discount is exhaustively defined. Additional returns and incentives may be gifts; that classification is not automatic. Actual fund return and distributor top-up return are expressly distinguished.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u7.1360","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The parenthetical exception attaches to discounts of fees or charges. A separately identifiable discount does not expressly exempt another benefit in a combined offer. Whether a fee-linked rebate actually qualifies as a discount remains unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected standard says should not offer. The proposed compliance predicate models conformity to that stated standard without converting it into the separate statutory offence. May be considered preserves judgment over classification.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The restriction concerns offering gifts during promotion. No effective date, transition period or payment deadline is supplied. The FAQ’s 30 September 2010 date identifies a source, not a commencement date.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The gift control is independently relevant even when an arrangement is not a structured product. The Code and supporting FAQ are identified but not supplied in full; section 103 authorisation or exemption does not establish satisfaction of the gift control.","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u9.1940","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u14.3675","db43e253bea18.u28.7987","db43e253bea18.u29.8110"],"status":"PROPOSED"}],"q