ount.","name":"benefit_is_fee_or_charge_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u13.2987"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or (not benefit_is_gift) benefit_is_fee_or_charge_discount)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_has_product_promotion_link)"},"local_id":"gift_component_control","questions":["Does the identified benefit qualify as a gift, and if so does it itself constitute a discount of fees or charges?","Does the referenced FAQ clarify treatment of rebates or inseparable combined benefits?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For the selected control, Paragraph 3.11 gift restriction for one offered benefit, true means that the in-scope benefit is either not a gift or qualifies for the fee-or-charge discount exception. False means that it is an in-scope gift outside that exception and fails the stated should-not-offer standard. This is a proposed interpretation of that control only; it does not determine compliance of other offer components, section 103 compliance or whole-firm compliance.","subject":"A separately identified benefit offered by a distributor during promotion to a client"}]}},"run_id":"run.0df6ab9ed0764d18b4c54714bd84a275"}